## What this oracle is

A QiForge oracle built on `@ixo/oracle-runtime`. The runtime handles HTTP, auth (UCAN), the agent graph, the LangGraph checkpointer, Matrix sync, and bundles 14 plugins by default. **You** ship: oracle identity, optional custom plugins, glue.

- **Organization:** {{org}}
- **Framework:** [QiForge](https://docs.ixo.world/build-an-oracle) (`@ixo/oracle-runtime`)
- **Public docs:** https://docs.ixo.world/build-an-oracle
- **AI-agent reference:** https://docs.ixo.world/build-an-oracle/for-ai-agents

## Layout

```
src/
├── main.ts        # bootstrap — calls createOracleApp({ config, plugins, … }) and listen()
├── config.ts      # oracle identity + system prompt (name, org, description, prompt)
└── plugins/       # custom plugins — one folder per plugin
```

Each custom plugin lives at `src/plugins/<name>/<name>.plugin.ts` with a colocated `<name>.plugin.test.ts`. The runtime auto-discovers nothing — every plugin must be passed in `plugins: []` in `main.ts`.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` | Hot-reload dev server (`tsx watch src/main.ts`). |
| `pnpm build` | TypeScript → `dist/`. |
| `pnpm start` | Run the compiled build. |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Type-check without emit. |
| `pnpm test` | Unit tests (vitest). |
| `qiforge-cli plugin new <name>` | Scaffold a new plugin into `src/plugins/<name>/`. |

## When the user asks "how do I…?"

A bundled skill at `.claude/skills/qiforge-oracle/SKILL.md` carries the dense how-to (plugin anatomy, recipes, env vars, the 14 bundled plugins, testing patterns). Trigger it for any oracle/plugin authoring question — the references load on demand so context stays light.

If the skill files don't cover it, fall back to:

1. The public docs at https://docs.ixo.world/build-an-oracle
2. `src/main.ts` and any existing plugin under `src/plugins/` (canonical local examples)

## Working with plugins

- Add a plugin via `qiforge-cli plugin new <name>` — produces a working skeleton with one tool + three tests.
- Register the new plugin in `src/main.ts` (the scaffold prints the exact snippet).
- The runtime validates the env at boot — every plugin's `configSchema` is merged into the composed schema. Missing required env vars fail fast with a clear error pointing at the plugin that needed them.

## Environment

`.env` holds secrets — never commit. `.env.example` lists every variable the bundled plugins and Tier-0 runtime need. Add plugin-specific variables to your plugin's `configSchema` (don't reach for `process.env` directly).
